consecutive block of length $\\ell \\in [2, k]$ has non-integer average (so <i>good</i> is equivalent to $(n-1)-$good). Then $n \\in \\{11, 13, 15, 17, 19, 21\\}$ have $7-$good permutations, $n=25$ has a $12-$good permutation, $n \\in \\{23, 27, 29, 33, 35, 37, 39\\}$ have $15-$good permutations."}],"has_more":false,"quota_max":300,"quota_remaining":298}